  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 115 AM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, rain continues to move southwest to northeast across \nthe region. Totals so far across central SD have been significantly \nhigher due to convection, with 2-3 inches so far across Corson \ncounty. Precipitation is expected to end over central SD this \nmorning and continue over northeastern SD and west central MN \nthrough at least the afternoon hours. Temperatures around the area \ncurrently are in the low 60s with winds around 10 mph out of the \nsouth. Chance of an additional half inch through the rest of the\nday is 60-80% for areas east of a line from Eureka to \nGettysburg to Huron. \n\nTemperatures through the middle of the week will be slightly above \naverage with highs in the 70s. Highs for the end of the week into \nthe weekend will be around to slightly below average, in the 60s. \nModels are starting to show a slight warm up again for the beginning \nof next work week. Our next best chance for precipitation will be \nSaturday as a shortwave/weak low moves across central ND. PoPs max \nout around 30% and are concentrated mainly along and north of Hwy \n12. Winds Friday afternoon will gust up to 30 mph west river, with \nsome locally higher gusts up to 35 mph in south central SD.",
